WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.732
Meanwhile, what happened to Edward during Tom's first days as king?

2
00:00:06.733 --> 00:00:09.723
Where did he go when he disappeared?

3
00:00:09.724 --> 00:00:15.821
Edward left the inn with the young man who'd brought the message he said was from Miles.

4
00:00:15.822 --> 00:00:22.680
As they walked toward the bridge and the woods, the man with the eye patch followed them.

5
00:00:22.681 --> 00:00:27.432
But he was careful to keep out of Edward's sight.

6
00:00:27.433 --> 00:00:34.874
After a few minutes of walking in the woods, Edward sat down on a tree stump and refused to move.

7
00:00:34.875 --> 00:00:39.938
"If Miles wants to talk, he should come to me

8
00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:44.755
!" Edward picked up a stone and gave it an angry

9
00:00:44.756 --> 00:00:47.223
toss. The young man looked

10
00:00:47.224 --> 00:00:52.462
surprised. "You want to sit here and wait while your friend lies

11
00:00:52.463 --> 00:00:57.522
wounded?" "Wounded? You didn't mention that Miles was

12
00:00:57.523 --> 00:01:01.243
wounded!" Edward's attitude instantly changed, and he hopped up.

13
00:01:01.244 --> 00:01:03.754
"We must hurry to him!"

14
00:01:03.755 --> 00:01:11.457
"Not so fast." The young man, whose name was Frank, studied the bare trees around them.

15
00:01:11.458 --> 00:01:15.297
"What are you looking for?" Edward said impatiently.

16
00:01:15.298 --> 00:01:17.934
"We have to get going!"

17
00:01:17.935 --> 00:01:25.074
"Aha! There's one!" Frank pointed to a small rag tied to a branch.

18
00:01:25.075 --> 00:01:30.427
"We need to follow the markers to the old farm."

19
00:01:30.428 --> 00:01:36.425
After a while they came to a clearing with a burned-out house and a ruined barn.

20
00:01:36.426 --> 00:01:39.598
Frank stopped outside the barn.

21
00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:44.689
"Miles! Where are you?" Edward called, but no one answered.

22
00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:50.524
He looked around in confusion. "Something's not right here."

23
00:01:50.525 --> 00:01:58.088
Frank burst into laughter as the man with the eye patch joined them.

24
00:01:58.089 --> 00:02:02.817
"It was almost too easy to trick him," Frank said to the man.

25
00:02:02.818 --> 00:02:06.771
"Who are you?" Edward asked the man.

26
00:02:06.772 --> 00:02:10.595
"Stop pretending that you don't recognize your own father."

27
00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:14.543
John Canty removed his eye patch.

28
00:02:14.544 --> 00:02:17.806
"You aren't my father," Edward said.

29
00:02:17.807 --> 00:02:23.604
"My father is dead, and I'm King Edward!"

30
00:02:23.605 --> 00:02:27.486
"It's clear that something's wrong with your mind.

31
00:02:27.487 --> 00:02:31.114
I hate to punish you, but if you provoke me, I will."

32
00:02:31.115 --> 00:02:37.441
John shook his fist at Edward. "Now, where are your mother and sister?

33
00:02:37.442 --> 00:02:41.445
They didn't come to our meeting place on the bridge."

34
00:02:41.446 --> 00:02:45.750
"They're at the palace, of course," Edward said.

35
00:02:45.751 --> 00:02:51.091
John groaned in frustration.

36
00:02:51.092 --> 00:02:56.840
While John and Frank talked, Edward wandered into the barn.

37
00:02:56.841 --> 00:03:03.607
Lying down on a pile of straw, he thought of his dead father and wept.

38
00:03:03.608 --> 00:03:07.691
He was soon asleep.

39
00:03:07.692 --> 00:03:13.506
*** When Edward woke up, it was dark, and a campfire was burning outside the barn.

40
00:03:13.507 --> 00:03:17.389
Gathered around the fire was a small group of people.

41
00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:25.072
A man tossed away his crutches, laughing about pretending to be lame.

42
00:03:25.073 --> 00:03:31.168
Another man emptied a woman's purse and handed the contents to the group's leader.

43
00:03:31.169 --> 00:03:33.322
"It's a gang of beggars and thieves!"

44
00:03:33.323 --> 00:03:39.921
Edward thought as he watched from inside the barn. "They're outlaws!"

45
00:03:39.922 --> 00:03:47.031
"So, John Canty, what brings you back to your old friends?" the leader asked.

46
00:03:47.032 --> 00:03:53.930
"Well, Ruffler, I made the mistake of injuring a priest, and now the law is after me," John said.

47
00:03:53.931 --> 00:03:57.984
"I had to flee the city, or they'd throw me in jail."

48
00:03:57.985 --> 00:04:03.113
"You don't want to go to jail," said the man who'd tossed away the crutches.

49
00:04:03.114 --> 00:04:10.708
"I ended up in jail after the king seized my farm to graze his sheep."

50
00:04:10.709 --> 00:04:14.890
The group nodded in agreement as the man continued his story.

51
00:04:14.891 --> 00:04:23.165
"My wife died, and I don't know where my children are—or if they're even alive."

52
00:04:23.166 --> 00:04:26.317
The man struggled to control his emotions.

53
00:04:26.318 --> 00:04:32.372
"I was sent to jail for stealing food, but I escaped.

54
00:04:32.373 --> 00:04:36.126
If I'm caught, I'll be hanged."

55
00:04:36.127 --> 00:04:38.968
Edward strode out of the barn.

56
00:04:38.969 --> 00:04:44.482
"You will not be hanged, and your land will be returned!

57
00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:50.355
As of today, the cruel reign of my father is over."

58
00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:55.123
There was a murmur of surprise among the group.

59
00:04:55.124 --> 00:04:58.424
"And who are you?" Ruffler asked.

60
00:04:58.425 --> 00:05:01.837
"I am King Edward!"

61
00:05:01.838 --> 00:05:08.663
A wild burst of laughter met that announcement.

62
00:05:08.664 --> 00:05:14.756
Edward was outraged. "Is this how you greet your king?"

63
00:05:14.757 --> 00:05:18.165
"Pay no attention to my son," John said.

64
00:05:18.166 --> 00:05:21.928
"He's suffering from a strange illness." But

65
00:05:21.929 --> 00:05:23.909
it was too late. Some

66
00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:28.070
men grabbed Edward and set him on a barrel for a throne. They

67
00:05:28.071 --> 00:05:33.925
crowned him with a tin basin and gave him a ragged blanket for a robe. "Long

68
00:05:33.926 --> 00:05:41.548
live the king!" the group shouted as they mocked Edward. ***

69
00:05:41.549 --> 00:05:48.845
As for Miles, he frantically searched all day for Edward but couldn't find the boy.

70
00:05:48.846 --> 00:05:53.958
Toward evening he gave up and went to an inn.

71
00:05:53.959 --> 00:05:59.057
Eating his supper, Miles thought some more about where Edward might be.

72
00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:04.012
"Edward didn't like the house on Offal Street, so he wouldn't return there.

73
00:06:04.013 --> 00:06:10.297
He's probably headed for my family's home because that's where we were supposed to go."

74
00:06:10.298 --> 00:06:20.026
The next morning Miles started for Hendon Hall, hoping to find Edward along the way.

